# Why every setting, env var, header and command this gateway uses is here.
#
# The rule, from the published methodology: a setting may appear only if it is needed to boot the
# process at all, to point an upstream at the test mock instead of a real provider, to expose an
# ingress path the matrix exercises, or to bind the port and cores the rig requires. One claim per
# line: <pattern> <boot|upstream|ingress|bind>. Nothing machine-checks this file: the shell lint
# that read these claims was deleted in 1127cf1, so it is a reviewed disclosure kept in step with
# the config by hand.
#
# Migrated from GW_CONFIG_WHY in the shell-era gateway.sh (deleted in 1127cf1).
PORT       bind      # the port the harness drives
OPENAI_BASE_URL    upstream  # each provider adapter has its own base-URL override; all -> the mock
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL upstream  # the path segment is the mock's provider marker, so boot-time model
GEMINI_BASE_URL    upstream  # discovery gets that provider's OWN catalog, and GoModel 404s a model
                             # not in the catalog it discovered at boot
BEDROCK_BASE_URL   upstream
BEDROCK_MODELS     upstream  # bedrock discovery is a SigV4 control-plane call the mock does not
OPENAI_API_KEY    boot   # a provider with no key is not configured (dummy; the mock ignores it)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY boot
GEMINI_API_KEY    boot
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID     boot
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY boot
AWS_REGION            boot
